From 5f8a9860407d1e7f7220e8b9f9fd462aea4ac39e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ed <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:05:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] ASoC: apple: aop_t8140: T6050 variant

A per-SoC HwConfig in the T8140 AOP audio driver, apple,t6050-aop-audio:
- no low-power microphone: it is exclave-owned on T6050, so no source
  ring, no card of the driver's own, and the fabric is not raised
  through it (with_fabric_raised runs its closure directly);
- no AP power domains: the audio PMGR domains are no_ps in the J714c
  ADT, power_up is a no-op, and each front-end attaches its stream's
  service and requests pw0 before its first DMA channel request, since
  the firmware powers the base-ns ADMAC;
- the speaker back-end is an MCA serializer stream like the jack's: six
  channels, 24-in-32-bit samples, no float32 copy path, and its capture
  is the amplifiers' V/I sense (12 x 16-bit) on the speaker service's
  own RX channel instead of the tap service;
- front-end DAIs j714-pcm-0..2, DMA names spkr, spkr-sense, cout, cin.
T8140 keeps its behaviour behind the same table.

rust/bindings: SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE for the sense stream.

Not yet known: when the firmware powers the base-ns fabric, so the
first DMA channel request may still stall; the serializer format the
amps and the jack codec must be set to (macaudio's default I2S IB_IF
is kept).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
[port to integration/aurora (aurora-j716s 6d9f1ec652a6): the driver is
 aop_t8140.rs, a backend of aop_audio.rs, here; the compatible goes into
 aop_audio.rs's table as AopVariant::T8140(&HW_T6050) and probe takes
 the HwConfig. The J714c DT, j714c.config and the J714 macaudio entry
 are board-specific and dropped.]
